// The 5 fae reward outcomes — what taking (or not taking) a fae gift does to the world.
//
// Ported verbatim from F:\NewRepo\crates\forge-reactions\src\fae_ethics.rs:24-32.
//
// ── THE STRUCTURE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Five lanes, each SIGNED: -/0/+ is a balanced trit, with permyriad magnitude on
// top. Five lanes x three states = 3^5 = 243, the exact shape of
// `forge_core_v3::atom::TritCell5D` (atom.rs:17, TRITS_PER_BYTE=5, 3^5==243
// asserted at :144). PARARITY.md §3 Cor. 2 is why a zero can exist at all:
// (m,k)=(1,1) is the only orbit type that carries a neutral.
//
// Sign vectors (own, oblig, crown, hostil, ecol):
//   Claimed    [+, 0, +, +, +]
//   Bargained  [+, +, +, -, 0]
//   Gifted     [-, +, -, -, -]
//   Stolen     [+, 0, +, +, +]     <- identical signature to Claimed
//   Refused    [-, -, -, -, -]
//
// TWO THINGS THE DATA SAYS, both preserved rather than flattened:
//
// 1. STOLEN AND CLAIMED SHARE ONE SIGN VECTOR. They differ only in magnitude and
//    in `shimmer_detectable`, which is true for Stolen ALONE across all five rows.
//    Stealing IS claiming — louder, and the only one that leaves a trace. A schema
//    storing only signs would merge them; one storing only magnitudes would lose
//    the trit. Both are stored.
//
// 2. CLAIMED -> REFUSED IS NOT AN EXACT NEGATION. Four lanes flip cleanly
//    (ownership, crown, hostility, ecology). Obligation does NOT: Claimed carries
//    0 and Refused carries -500. Claiming takes on no bond; refusing actively
//    sheds one. The mirror is real on four lanes and asymmetric on the fifth, and
//    the tests assert exactly that rather than the tidier claim.
(
    outcomes: [
        (
            outcome: Claimed,
            ownership_pressure_q: 2500,
            obligation_pressure_q: 0,
            crown_temptation_q: 2000,
            fae_hostility_q: 2000,
            ecology_pressure_q: 500,
            shimmer_detectable: false,
        ),
        (
            outcome: Bargained,
            ownership_pressure_q: 500,
            obligation_pressure_q: 2500,
            crown_temptation_q: 500,
            fae_hostility_q: -500,
            ecology_pressure_q: 0,
            shimmer_detectable: false,
        ),
        (
            outcome: Gifted,
            ownership_pressure_q: -1000,
            obligation_pressure_q: 500,
            crown_temptation_q: -2000,
            fae_hostility_q: -2000,
            ecology_pressure_q: -1000,
            shimmer_detectable: false,
        ),
        (
            // The only detectable row. Same trit signature as Claimed, larger in
            // every magnitude, and it leaves a shimmer the world can read.
            outcome: Stolen,
            ownership_pressure_q: 3000,
            obligation_pressure_q: 0,
            crown_temptation_q: 1500,
            fae_hostility_q: 3500,
            ecology_pressure_q: 1000,
            shimmer_detectable: true,
        ),
        (
            outcome: Refused,
            ownership_pressure_q: -1500,
            obligation_pressure_q: -500,
            crown_temptation_q: -2500,
            fae_hostility_q: -3000,
            ecology_pressure_q: -2000,
            shimmer_detectable: false,
        ),
    ],
)
